set covers multiple agent scenarios and aims to enhance model performance in autonomous decision-making, tool usage, code generation, and interactive task handling. We reselected some of the training queries from the NEX-N1 training dataset and regenerated the responses based on DeepSeek-V3.1-Nex-N1. This data can provide a reference for the community to train and develop new agent models.\n##   ⟨47⟩ Dataset Distribtion   \n| Category  | Value  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| agentic_code  | 24796  |  \n| agent  | 11749  |  \n| chat  | 2079  |  \n| html  | 8332  |  \n| tool_call  | 9737  |  \n| **Total**  | **69008**  |  \n##   ⟨48⟩ Dataset Structure \nEach example in the dataset contains the standard instruction-tuning data points as follow:\n  * `uuid` (str): a unique identifier\n  * `messages` (list): message format used for supervised fine-tuning (this contains systerm prompt, user prompt, assistant responses and tool response)\n  * `tools` (list): the list of tool definitions, where each definition includes a tool name, a description, and parameters defined by properties.\n  * `generator` (str): the model name for generating responses.\n\n\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    191\nTotal file size: 10.1 GB\n##  Paper for Aoneesh/agent-sft\n#### Nex-N1: Agentic Models Trained via a Unified Ecosystem for Large-Scale Environment Construction Paper • 2512.04987 • Published Dec 4, 2025 • 85 ⟨50⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨53⟩ Privacy⟨54⟩ About⟨55⟩ Careers⟨56⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\nThe table displays a preview with only the first rows.\n",
